WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.234
-Welcome to the show.
-Thank you.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.701
-Jamie, It's great to meet you.

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.434
It's so nice to meet you.
I'm happy you're here.

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.167
-It's a pleasure to be here.
I'm so grateful.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:08.701
Thank you so much, Jimmy.

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.300
-I have a lot to talk to you.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.033
congratulations on everything
with "Stranger Things."

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:13.400
I mean, it's the biggest thing.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.434
You joined the season this year
as the villain, as Vecna.

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:20.133
You instantly became
a fan favorite.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.601
People love you.
And...

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:25.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:28.167
There it is.
How much of a...

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:35.367
I love that -- did you ever
think that you would ever get

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:38.167
to play a character and wear all
these prosthetics? I mean...

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:39.367
-Absolutely not.

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:40.767
I mean, I never even imagined
I would be on

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:44.133
a show like this, let alone
playing this thing.

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:48.200
Yeah, it's amazing.
It was just such a blessing.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.567
The whole thing feels like such
a whirlwind since I got it.

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:52.601
It's bizarre.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:55.167
-How much is CGI
and how much is real?

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.968
-It's about 90 percent real.

00:00:56.968 --> 00:01:00.167
So it takes about eight hours
to put the whole thing on,

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:01.567
so I have to kind of...
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:03.067
Thank you, I appreciate that.

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:04.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:05.801
I feel sorry for me, too.

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:08.567
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:11.534
-I'm working with Barry Gower,
who's amazing, who works on

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:13.200
"Game of Thrones"
and "The Witcher."

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.133
Duncan Jarman, Mike McCash,
Nicks and Eric Garcia.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:18.601
Shoutout to those guys.
Thank you so much.

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:19.734
-Yeah.

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:21.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:24.067
-Um, yeah, so it's about eight
hours in the process.

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:27.100
And we start at like 3:00 A.M.
in the morning

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.000
to be ready for about
10:00, and then --

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.634
-And then you have to act.
-And then I have to act, yeah.

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:33.367
-And how fast is it to take off?

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:35.334
-It's about an hour,
hour and a half, yeah.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:38.300
-Yeah. I like these random
photos they took of you

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.734
behind the scenes,
like backstage.

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:42.968
Your fellow cast members
who love you so much.

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:45.968
They just take photos of you
and post them on the Internet.

00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:48.400
Here is one of Vecna
drinking a Starbucks,

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.767
which is just thought...

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:56.133
[ Laughs ]

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:57.834
I just love that.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:02:00.067
You got to have a little
caffeine in there, yeah.

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:01.133
-Always, yeah.
-Always.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:02.901
-That's only way
to get through. really.

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:06.067
Powered by caffeine, Vecna.
There you go.

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:09.467
-And when you do the -- on top
of the physical transformation,

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.801
the voice of Vecna,
did you always know

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:13.567
which voice
you were going to go with?

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:16.434
-No. It took -- it took
a few months to get right.

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:19.300
We had to read through
in March of 2020,

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.367
and I had been doing a bit of
work on Vecna and on Henry.

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.868
I only got the job in January,
so I had kind of February

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:26.400
to prepare for it.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.901
We did the read through,
and I was there

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:29.434
kind of at the table
reading with everyone.

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:32.067
I sat behind Milly,
and I was doing the voice

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:34.567
and it started in this
like very kind of like

00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:36.934
nasally kind of area,
kind of more like

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:39.367
Freddie Krueger
and it just wasn't landing.

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:42.400
So I went home and worked on it,
did a bunch of reference work

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.968
on like "Hellraiser"

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:45.501
and Doug Bradley,
in particularly.

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:48.067
And said that, you know, this
deep, booming voice

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.701
kind of comes out
of the darkness.

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:51.934
And I was like, "Oh, yeah.
You can tell."

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:54.100
-Yeah.
You're getting somewhere.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.267
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
I like that.

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:56.901
-I loved it.
It was amazing.

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:58.901
So I just kind
of worked on that,

00:02:58.901 --> 00:03:01.701
and I'm a singer so I kind
of just relaxed myself,

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:02.901
relaxed my larynx.

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:03.934
You're a singer, so you know
what it's like.

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:05.000
Relax your --
I've seen you sing.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.334
You can sing.
Don't give me that.

00:03:06.334 --> 00:03:07.767
-No, I mean, you're a singer.

00:03:07.767 --> 00:03:10.801
I sing. I sing,
but you're a singer.

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:12.133
That's the difference, yeah.

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:14.534
You actually have a new song
coming out August 12th.

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:15.868
-I do, yes.

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:18.534
-August 12th.

00:03:18.534 --> 00:03:20.067
It's called "I Am."

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:21.067
-Yes.
-Congrats.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.400
Are you excited for that?

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.601
-I'm so excited.

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:25.234
Everything just feels
not real right now.

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:26.567
-It's all happening.
-Yes.

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:28.434
-I mean, that's soon.
August 12th.

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:30.100
-Yeah, it's like two weeks away.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.434
-Yeah, so guys, look for "I Am,"
who's coming out,

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:33.734
yeah, Jamie's new song.

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:36.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:38.801
And then on top of that,
I heard that you're also

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:40.801
filming a movie
with Kevin Costner.

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:44.367
-I am.
Yes, you get the exclusive.

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:48.200
I'm doing a Western saga
with Mr. Kevin Costner.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.067
I'll be -- Yeah, I know, wild.

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:52.601
I'll be in, I think,
Utah in October

00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:54.968
riding a horse
wearing a Stetson.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.234
-I mean, come on!
-I know, I know.

00:03:56.234 --> 00:03:58.067
-That's a dream right there.
With Kevin Costner?

00:03:58.067 --> 00:04:00.334
-Yeah, yeah.
-Who's also a good musician.

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:02.400
-Amazing musician.
-Yeah, you should jam with him.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.968
-I heard some of it
like two weeks ago.

00:04:03.968 --> 00:04:05.000
-It's good.
-I was in a fitting,

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.267
and I just heard it,
it's amazing.

00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:07.534
He's so talented.

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:08.801
-I was listening
to your stuff today.

00:04:08.801 --> 00:04:11.033
I know you're in a band,
I listened to your songs.

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:13.634
But also I found out
this very cool things.

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:14.934
I didn't know.

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:18.100
I knew the voice
before I heard Vecna.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.167
And I realized that you're
also the voice

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:22.501
of Skiff from
"Thomas &amp; Friends."

00:04:22.501 --> 00:04:23.834
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:23.834 --> 00:04:24.968
-This is real.

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:27.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.934
This is true.

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:30.968
This is true.
-Yeah.

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:33.367
-It's hard to believe that these

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:34.868
are both the same person.

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:36.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.501 --> 00:04:37.868
Yeah, Vecna and...

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:39.200
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.634
[ Applause ]

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:43.367
-And just for fun, we wanted to
see what would sound like

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:46.400
if you had used your Vecna
voice for Skiff.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:47.801
-Oh, my goodness.
-Check this out.

00:04:47.801 --> 00:04:49.167
-Okay.

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:54.734
-[ Deep voice ] It is time
that I bring you to join me.

00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:56.400
-There you go.
It's very frightening.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.334
-[ Laughs ]
-Skiff.

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:00.601
[ Applause ]

00:05:00.601 --> 00:05:03.334
Fans of "Stranger Things"
have called Vecna

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:05.934
the scariest character
that they have ever seen.

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:07.367
He's pretty terrifying.

00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:10.467
I was wondering if you wouldn't
mind doing the Vecna voice

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:12.467
for us right now.

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:14.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:15.601
-For you Jimmy, anything.

00:05:15.601 --> 00:05:16.868
I got you, I got you.

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:18.167
-But here's what we did.

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:20.701
What we did, we put some
of your lines on cue cards.

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.367
-Okay.
-Okay, and the twist

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:24.734
is that there are all things
that Vecna would never say.

00:05:24.734 --> 00:05:26.167
Okay.

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:27.267
-Whenever you're ready.

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:28.634
Roots, can you give us
a little music?

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:30.167
[ Sinister music playing ]

00:05:30.167 --> 00:05:31.567
-I'm sorry about this everyone.

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:36.467
[ Deep voice ] I'm just a girl

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:43.133
standing in front of a boy,
asking him to love her.

00:05:43.133 --> 00:05:46.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:46.734 --> 00:05:49.701
-Try this on, try this on.
This is it.

00:05:49.701 --> 00:05:52.334
-I'm cuckoo for Cocoa Puffs.

00:05:52.334 --> 00:05:54.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:57.934 --> 00:06:01.834
Jack, oh, Jack.

00:06:01.834 --> 00:06:05.400
I want you to draw me like one
of your French girls.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:10.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:14.200
♪♪

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.400
[ Normal voice ] This is a daily
affirmation for Vecna, okay?

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.234 --> 00:06:20.334
[ Deep voice ] I am strong.

00:06:20.334 --> 00:06:22.934
I am beautiful.

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:24.400
I am kind.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.534
-Yeah.

00:06:25.534 --> 00:06:28.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:28.801 --> 00:06:30.934
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:30.934 --> 00:06:32.400
-You see it?

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:33.467
-Alright, this is for you,
Jimmy.

00:06:33.467 --> 00:06:35.868
-Okay, I really beg you
do this one.

00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:39.400
♪♪

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:44.968
In a minute, I'ma need a
sentimental man

00:06:44.968 --> 00:06:47.434
or woman to pump you up.

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:50.734
Feeling fussy, walkin
in my balenci-ussy's

00:06:50.734 --> 00:06:54.100
tryna bring out the fabulous.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:56.434 --> 00:06:58.200
-That is how you do it!

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.968
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:59.968 --> 00:07:03.367
Here's Jamie Campbell Bower as
Vecna in "Stranger Things."

00:07:03.367 --> 00:07:06.367
Take a look at this!

00:07:06.367 --> 00:07:09.734
-But in the end,

00:07:09.734 --> 00:07:13.834
he could not control us.

00:07:13.834 --> 00:07:17.400
He could not shape us.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:20.834
He could not change us.

00:07:20.834 --> 00:07:26.067
Do you not see, Eleven.

00:07:26.067 --> 00:07:31.734
He did not make me into this.

00:07:31.734 --> 00:07:33.200
You did.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.868
♪♪

00:07:36.868 --> 00:07:38.767
-Jamie Campbell Bower, everyone.

00:07:38.767 --> 00:07:42.734
Season four of "Stranger Things"
streaming now on Netflix.

00:07:42.734 --> 00:07:45.467
August 12th, "I Am."

00:07:45.467 --> 00:07:48.167
We'll be right back with a
performance from King Princess!

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:49.334
Stick around, everybody!

